course: dictionary
lesson: 499
title: Asleep: sleeping, or numb
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Asleep has two meanings. The first is the one you know: sleeping. «Stopping screens at a fixed time, with a quiet wind-down before bed, helps children fall asleep faster.» Here fall asleep means starting to sleep.
explain: The second meaning is about your body. If you sit on your foot for too long, it goes numb and tingly, and you can say «My foot is asleep». Nothing is really sleeping; the foot just cannot feel properly for a while.
explain: Check the words around asleep to see which meaning fits. It often comes after a verb such as be or fall, as in «fast asleep» or «sound asleep». If a person or animal is sleeping, use meaning 1. If it is an arm or leg, use meaning 2.
fact: Asleep means sleeping.
fact: Of an arm or leg, asleep means numb and tingly because you sat on it too long.
fact: Useful phrases: fall asleep, fast asleep, sound asleep, half asleep, asleep at the wheel.
fact: Children need about 9 to 12 hours of sleep, and a regular bedtime helps them fall asleep.
fact: Dolphins can be asleep with only half their brain at a time, so the other half stays awake to come up for air.
exercise: «Stopping screens at a fixed time helps children fall asleep faster.» What does asleep mean here? | Numb and tingly from sitting still | *Sleeping | Wet from the bath | Wide awake and ready for school
exercise: Maya says, «My foot is asleep» after sitting cross-legged for an hour. What does she mean? | Her foot is fast asleep under the blanket | Her foot is sore from a fall | Her foot is cold and wet | *Her foot is numb and tingly
exercise: Which sentence uses asleep to mean sleeping? | The bath was asleep and cold. | *She was fast asleep in her bed by nine. | He sat on his arm for an hour, and it went asleep. | Asleep, he ran to the bus stop.
test: In «Sleeping Beauty was asleep for a hundred years», what does asleep mean? | Numb and tingly | *Sleeping | Wet and cold | Awake and busy
test: «Drivers must not fall asleep.» What does this rule warn about? | Drivers must always wear a hat | *Drivers must not go to sleep while driving | Drivers must not sit on their arms | Drivers must keep the windows shut
exam: Which meaning fits «My leg is asleep», and why? | *Numb and tingly, because it has been sat on too long | Wide awake and running around the field | Fast asleep in bed under a duvet | Sleeping, because the leg is tired and needs rest
